    "explanation": "To both parties: this dispute is decided on the trip's own numbers, and the route-deviation test is not met.\n\n1. The POL-RD-01 gate fails. The governing measurement is the GPS trace (EV-GPS-00102, weight 1.00), which records trace_distance_km = 21.79 km; the trip record's actual_distance_km = 21.8 km is a rounded convenience copy of the same measurement and may NOT be cited for the threshold test. Against the platform's stored optimal distance of 20.4 km (EV-TRIP-00102), the excess is 1.39 km, or 6.81% of optimal. POL-RD-01 requires BOTH an excess greater than 0.8 km absolute AND greater than 20% of optimal. The absolute limb (1.39 km) is cleared, but the percentage limb (6.81% vs 20%) fails by a wide margin, so no deviation is established and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The trace that carries this number is unimpaired: 193 fixes, a 10-second sample interval, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0.0. It satisfies none of POL-RD-07 (a)-(c), so POL-RD-07 impair-handling and POL-RD-10(3) are not engaged.\n\n2. The rider's $7.00 claim has no foundation in this trip's arithmetic. Even the platform's own POL-RD-02 recomputation — which only runs where a deviation is established, and none is — would yield recomputed_fare 27.46 against charged_total 29.91, a difference of $2.45, not $7.00. The rider's figure is a round-number preference, not a measured loss.\n\n3. On the driver's account that the BKE was congested (chat message at 11:29:04 and the counterparty statement): both are noted, but an assertion of bad traffic unsupported by a traffic_advisory ID carries no weight under POL-RD-08, and in any event the driver does not need it, because there is no established deviation to excuse. I record that EV-ADVIS-00102-01 is MISSING (weight_multiplier 0.00, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT, BLOCKING) and that no LTA advisory covers the BKE / Upper Bukit Timah corridor in the trip window — but its absence is immaterial here. It does not fire POL-RD-10(5), because no exculpatory clause is invoked against it: the driver does not rely on POL-RD-03 as a ground of decision, so that trigger does not arise. The absence is citable as evidence of nothing rather than a gap that changes the outcome.\n\n4. The single chat message is the driver's own. No rider reply is recorded (delivered 11:29:05, read 11:29:40, no response) and chat_message.waypoint_hint is null, so POL-RD-04 is unavailable on its own terms — a driver's request for permission is not the rider's instruction. Separately, the fare was charged on 21.8 km against a trace of 21.79 km, so no distance was left unbilled and no driver compensation arises under the POL-RD-04 shortfall limb.\n\n5. Billing integrity (POL-RD-09(4)): the fare carries no ERP/toll lines, no airport surcharge, and every charge line has a counterpart in the trace and trip record. No standalone correction is due, whether or not a deviation exists.\n\n6. Repeat-deviation pattern (POL-RD-06): the driver's deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 640, so neither limb of the pattern test is met, and there is no material deviation to uplift. No POL-RD-06(c) conduct referral follows.\n\nOutcome: NO_ACTION. Under POL-GEN-03 that outcome is party-relative: on this rider-filed dispute it leaves the present state exactly as it stands — payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00. No escalation trigger under POL-RD-10 fires (confidence is above the 0.70 floor; identifiers and timestamps are consistent; the trace is unimpaired; no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing artifact; no charge line is unmatched), and no clause produces a referral. Both accounts are plausible descriptions of the same drive; the policy simply does not make a 1.39 km (6.81%) excess refundable."
