    "explanation": "Outcome: NO_ACTION — the $29.91 fare stands, with no refund to the rider and no compensation to the driver.\n\nWhy the rider's route-deviation claim fails. POL-RD-01 sets a single numeric gate and both its limbs must pass. The governing distance is gps_trace.trace_distance_km (EV-GPS-00102) at 21.79 km; trip_record.actual_distance_km (EV-TRIP-00102, 21.8 km) is a rounded convenience copy that the clause forbids citing for the threshold test. Against the stored optimal of 20.4 km the excess is 1.39 km, which is 6.81% of optimal. The excess clears the 0.8 km absolute limb but not the >20% limb, and because the two tests are cumulative, no deviation is established 'however the rider characterises the trip'. The rider's time point (32 min against 27 min) does not help: POL-RD-01 measures excess distance, not duration.\n\nThe measurement is reliable. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07 — 193 fixes at a 10 s interval, 100% coverage, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0.0, so none of limbs (a) to (c) is met. There is no POL-RD-10(3) escalation and the excess is measured from a clean, weight-1.0 artifact.\n\nThe driver's traffic assertion. The driver says the BKE was slow near Dairy Farm and that he came off via Upper Thomson. That does not change the outcome, because no deviation was established and POL-RD-03 exoneration is therefore never reached. The LTA advisory he would need, EV-ADVIS-00102-01, is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue MISSING_ARTIFACT; its absence is citable but immaterial here. No exculpatory clause is invoked against it as a ground of decision — the driver's own brief disclaims POL-RD-03 — so no POL-RD-10(5) escalation fires, and the rider's escalation argument to that effect was struck by the referee for not disclosing the artifact's impairment and cannot be reinstated. The case is decided at the POL-RD-01 gate on clean evidence and nothing requires a human reviewer.\n\nBilling integrity is clean